##STOREFRONT SETUP – GUMROAD
Once your ebook is designed and ready, you need a platform where customers can purchase and download it. Gumroad allows you to create a digital product listing, accept payments and automatically deliver your ebook to buyers.



Create a Gumroad Account -
Visit Gumroad.
Sign up using your email address.
Complete your account details.
Set up your creator profile with a name, profile picture and short description.
Complete the required identity and payment verification.



Create Your First Product -
Open your Gumroad dashboard.
Navigate to the Products section.
Select the option to create a new product.
Choose Digital Product as your product type.
Enter your ebook's title.
Upload your final PDF file.



Set Your Ebook Pricing - 
Research the prices of similar ebooks.
Consider the value and usefulness of your content.
Start with an affordable price to encourage initial purchases.
Experiment with pricing as you receive customer feedback.
Consider offering discounts or promotional pricing.

For example, you could initially price an ebook at $10, depending on its content and target audience.



Create Your Product Description - 
Your product description should explain why someone should purchase your ebook.

Include:
What the ebook is about.
Who should purchase it.
Which problems it helps solve.
What readers will learn.
What is included in the ebook.
The format and delivery method.

Focus on the benefits and outcomes rather than simply listing chapters.



Design Your Product Cover and Preview - 
Create an attractive ebook cover using Canva.
Prepare a product thumbnail or promotional mockup.
Include a few preview pages to show potential customers what they will receive.
Maintain the same branding as your Threads profile.



Configure Product Delivery - 
Upload the final PDF to Gumroad.
Add a short thank-you message for customers.
Review the product's delivery settings.
Configure any additional product options you need.
Test the purchase and download experience before promoting your ebook.



Add Your Gumroad Link to Threads - 
Copy your Gumroad product URL.
Open your Threads profile.
Select Edit Profile.
Add the product URL to your profile links.
Save your changes.
Open the link to ensure it directs visitors to the correct product page.



Things to Keep in Mind - 
Maintain consistent branding across Gumroad and Threads.
Write an honest and compelling product description.
Check Gumroad's current transaction fees and payment availability in your country.
Make sure your payment and identity verification requirements are completed.
Keep your ebook updated when necessary.
Don't make unrealistic promises about the results customers will achieve.



Useful tools - 
Gumroad – Digital product storefront and delivery.
Canva – Ebook covers and product mockups.
